;; A 9x9 Latin square: a grid in which each row and each column has nine different values,
;; like a sudoku without the boxes and without clues. Any such grid will do, and there are plenty.
;;
;; This version: 4-bit bit-vectors from 1 to 9.
;; Z3 5.4.1 takes a few hundredths of a second: bit-vectors are turned into a SAT problem.
;;
;; Run it with the z3 command line, for example with a 60-second limit:
;;     z3 -T:60 examples/smt2/latin_square_bv.smt2
;; or run all three versions, timed, with examples/smt2/latin_squares.sh.
;; See examples/sudoku.pl, which uses an enumeration sort because of this.

